<article class="env-lemma" id="048W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/048W">Lemma <span data-tag="048W">83.5.9</span>.</a> In the situation of Definition <a href="/tag/048V" data-tag="048V">83.5.8</a>. A morphism $\phi : U \to X$ is set-theoretically $R$-invariant if and only if for any algebraically closed field $k$ over $B$ the map $U(k) \to X(k)$ is constant on orbits. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because the condition is supposed to hold for all algebraically closed fields over $B$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>